            subtitle: "고찰 순례의 길",
            korean: `<p><span class="korean-word" data-translation="traveling to ancient temples of Korea" data-pronunciation="한국의 고찰을 순례하노라면 [hangukui gochareul sullуеhanoraмyeon]">한국의 고찰을 순례하노라면</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="not only learning history" data-pronunciation="역사를 배울뿐더러 [yeoksareul baеulppundeoreo]">역사를 배울뿐더러</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="but also spiritually purified" data-pronunciation="영적으로 정화되거니와 [yeongjeоgeuro jeonghwadoegеoniwa]">영적으로 정화되거니와</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="this experience" data-pronunciation="이런 경험이야말로 [ireon gyeongheomiyamallo]">이런 경험이야말로</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="the true meaning of travel" data-pronunciation="여행의 참된 의미입니다 [yeohaengui chamdoen uimiimnida]">여행의 참된 의미입니다</span>.</p>
<p><span class="korean-word" data-translation="Haeinsa Temple's" data-pronunciation="해인사의 [haеinsa-ui]">해인사의</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="Tripitaka Koreana" data-pronunciation="팔만대장경은 [palman-daejanggyeongeun]">팔만대장경은</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="a World Heritage site, and" data-pronunciation="세계유산인 바 [segyeyusanin ba]">세계유산인 바</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="standing before it" data-pronunciation="그 앞에 서면 [geu ape seomyeon]">그 앞에 서면</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="a millennium of wisdom" data-pronunciation="천 년의 지혜가 [cheon nyeonui jihyega]">천 년의 지혜가</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="can be felt" data-pronunciation="느껴집니다 [neukkyеojipnida]">느껴집니다</span>.</p>
<p><span class="korean-word" data-translation="if one contemplates the meaning of pilgrimage" data-pronunciation="순례의 의미를 생각할진대 [sullуeui uimireul saenggakhalchindae]">순례의 의미를 생각할진대</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="physical movement" data-pronunciation="육체적 이동보다 [yukchеjeok idongboda]">육체적 이동보다</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="the inner journey" data-pronunciation="내면의 여정이야말로 [naemyеonui yеojeongiyamallo]">내면의 여정이야말로</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="is more important" data-pronunciation="더 중요한 바입니다 [deo jungyohan baimnida]">더 중요한 바입니다</span>.</p>
<p><span class="korean-word" data-translation="as long as temples exist" data-pronunciation="사찰이 존재하는 한 [sachari jonjaehaneun han]">사찰이 존재하는 한</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="people" data-pronunciation="사람들은 [saramdeureun]">사람들은</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="will come here" data-pronunciation="이곳을 찾을 바이니 [igoseul chajeul baini]">이곳을 찾을 바이니</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="therein" data-pronunciation="여기에 [yеogie]">여기에</span> <span class="korean-word" data-translation="lies the hope of humanity" data-pronunciation="인류의 희망이 있습니다 [illуuui huimangi itseumnida]">인류의 희망이 있습니다</span>.</p>`,
            translation: "Traveling to ancient temples of Korea, one not only learns history but is also spiritually purified — this is the true meaning of travel. The Tripitaka Koreana at Haeinsa Temple is a World Heritage site, and standing before it, one feels a millennium of wisdom. Contemplating the meaning of pilgrimage, one understands that the inner journey is more important than physical movement. As long as temples exist, people will come here — therein lies the hope of humanity.",
